[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3449356362","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112071#issuecomment-3449356362","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112071","id":3449356362,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NmQBK","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-27T03:26:06Z","updated_at":"2025-10-27T03:26:06Z","body":"The problem is you are grabbing the non-msaa buffer with [`get_color_layer()`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_renderscenebuffersrd.html#class-renderscenebuffersrd-method-get-color-layer) and then attempting to render to it. When MSAA is enabled, you should be grabbing the MSAA buffer. The second parameter to `get_color_layer()` controls whether you are grabbing the non-msaa buffer or the MSAA buffer. \n\nThis is the same reason behind your second issue. You are rendering to a different buffer than Godot. In post transparent, Godot will have resolved the MSAA buffer to the non-MSAA buffer, which is why it works there","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":n